WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:03.501
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to "The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:03.501 --> 00:00:05.267
You're here! "The Tonight Show"!

00:00:05.267 --> 00:00:08.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:09.968
Well, let's get to some news here.

00:00:09.968 --> 00:00:11.767
Guys, this weekend, President Biden

00:00:11.767 --> 00:00:13.100
returned to the White House

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:15.634
after a four-day trip to Ireland.

00:00:15.634 --> 00:00:18.434
Yeah, you can tell Biden really enjoyed his time in Ireland

00:00:18.434 --> 00:00:20.100
'cause today, instead of falling down

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.234
the steps of Air Force One, he river-danced down them.

00:00:22.234 --> 00:00:23.234
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.234 --> 00:00:26.133
Oh, eh -- ooh. Oh.

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:29.133
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:31.067
I always love watching someone fall up.

00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:32.868
I just think it's very rare.

00:00:32.868 --> 00:00:36.067
During his trip, Biden quoted his favorite Irish poet,

00:00:36.067 --> 00:00:38.434
which is different from Trump's favorite Irish quote,

00:00:38.434 --> 00:00:39.934
"They'll never get me Lucky Charms."

00:00:39.934 --> 00:00:42.601
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.601 --> 00:00:44.868
Yeah, I think Biden had a pretty good time in Ireland.

00:00:44.868 --> 00:00:47.033
On Friday night, he gave a big speech.

00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:48.501
And check out the welcome that he received

00:00:48.501 --> 00:00:50.501
when he walked on stage. This is real.

00:00:50.501 --> 00:00:51.868
-Joe Biden.

00:00:51.868 --> 00:00:53.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:53.334 --> 00:00:56.834
[ Dropkick Murphy's "I'm Shipping up to Boston" plays ]

00:00:56.834 --> 00:01:06.901
♪♪

00:01:06.901 --> 00:01:09.467
♪♪

00:01:09.467 --> 00:01:10.901
-Wow. -Come on.

00:01:10.901 --> 00:01:13.067
-Yeah. [ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:15.167
-The ovation was so loud, even Biden could hear it.

00:01:15.167 --> 00:01:16.367
It was amazing. [ Laughter ]

00:01:16.367 --> 00:01:18.801
Yeah, Biden walked out to the Irish punk band

00:01:18.801 --> 00:01:20.100
Dropkick Murphys.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.734
It was a pretty interesting song choice,

00:01:22.734 --> 00:01:24.367
but it makes more sense than the song

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:25.400
that he was originally planning

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:27.167
on walking out to listen to this.

00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:29.868
-Please welcome Joe Biden.

00:01:29.868 --> 00:01:31.267
[ Funky music plays ]

00:01:31.267 --> 00:01:33.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.434 --> 00:01:40.200
♪♪

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.634
-Of course.

00:01:42.634 --> 00:01:45.634
-That's -- [ Laughs ]

00:01:45.634 --> 00:01:49.334
-♪ Wow, wow, wow ♪

00:01:49.334 --> 00:01:54.901
-♪ Wow, wow, wow ♪ -♪ Wow, wow, wow ♪

00:01:54.901 --> 00:01:56.434
-'Course, Biden's not the only political figure

00:01:56.434 --> 00:01:58.801
who uses walk-out music to help set the mood.

00:01:58.801 --> 00:02:00.534
I'll show you what I mean. For instance,

00:02:00.534 --> 00:02:02.868
at other speeches, you could hear songs like

00:02:02.868 --> 00:02:04.634
"Insane in the Membrane"

00:02:04.634 --> 00:02:07.434
or "Bad Romance"

00:02:07.434 --> 00:02:10.767
or "Oops, I did it Again." -Oh!

00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:13.000
-Or "I Can't Get No Satisfaction."

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:15.300
-Oh! -And artists like

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.734
Ol' Dirty Bastard

00:02:16.734 --> 00:02:20.367
or "The Star-Spangled Banner," which I'm told by George Santos,

00:02:20.367 --> 00:02:22.167
was written by Francis Scott Santos.

00:02:22.167 --> 00:02:23.367
-Really? [ Laughter ]

00:02:23.367 --> 00:02:25.734
-Or the classic Eric Clapton song "Cocaine."

00:02:25.734 --> 00:02:27.868
Or -- [ Audience "Ohhs," Laughter ]

00:02:27.868 --> 00:02:29.400
Or ever since the Trump indictment,

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:30.501
some people are just playing this.

00:02:30.501 --> 00:02:31.934
-♪ Because I'm happy ♪

00:02:31.934 --> 00:02:34.934
-♪ Clap along if you feel like a room without a roof ♪

00:02:34.934 --> 00:02:38.300
-Yeah, people are just playing.

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:41.467
Some more political news. Guys, the 2024 campaign season

00:02:41.467 --> 00:02:44.000
is in full swing, and after months of attacks

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.534
from former president Trump,

00:02:45.534 --> 00:02:47.334
Florida Governor Ron DeSantis

00:02:47.334 --> 00:02:50.367
is finally fighting back with an attack ad against Trump.

00:02:50.367 --> 00:02:51.767
-Oh. -Watch this.

00:02:51.767 --> 00:02:53.334
-Trump should fight Democrats,

00:02:53.334 --> 00:02:57.133
not lie about Governor DeSantis. What happened to Donald Trump?

00:02:57.133 --> 00:02:59.234
-Ooh. -Ooh.

00:02:59.234 --> 00:03:00.968
-But Trump isn't backing down.

00:03:00.968 --> 00:03:04.000
In response, his super PAC just released an attack ad

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:06.067
based on a story. This is real, by the way.

00:03:06.067 --> 00:03:07.534
This is -- You saw this?

00:03:07.534 --> 00:03:09.100
-Yeah. -This is based on a story

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:12.033
that DeSantis once ate pudding with his fingers.

00:03:12.033 --> 00:03:13.534
Did you hear this? [ Laughter ]

00:03:13.534 --> 00:03:15.400
I'm not making this up. This is not a joke.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:18.467
-This is a real -This is a real attack ad.

00:03:18.467 --> 00:03:20.901
This -- This is this is real. Check this out.

00:03:20.901 --> 00:03:23.701
-Ron DeSantis loves sticking his fingers

00:03:23.701 --> 00:03:25.234
where they don't belong.

00:03:25.234 --> 00:03:27.334
And we're not just talking about pudding.

00:03:27.334 --> 00:03:30.667
-Oh. [ Audience groans ]

00:03:30.667 --> 00:03:32.067
-That's real. -Yeah.

00:03:32.067 --> 00:03:33.834
-That is real.

00:03:33.834 --> 00:03:36.000
Then the DeSantis super PAC replied with...

00:03:41.701 --> 00:03:43.701
Then the Trump super PAC was like...

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:53.534
Then the DeSantis ad said...

00:04:00.968 --> 00:04:03.033
Oh. [ Laughter ]

00:04:03.033 --> 00:04:05.000
Then Trump's ad said...

00:04:10.501 --> 00:04:12.901
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.901 --> 00:04:15.100
Then DeSantis's ad said...

00:04:20.167 --> 00:04:21.234
I mean... [ Laughter ]

00:04:21.234 --> 00:04:24.200
Then -- Then Trump's ad said...

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:31.133
And, finally, DeSantis's ad said...

00:04:33.033 --> 00:04:35.834
There you go. -Ohh!

00:04:35.834 --> 00:04:40.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:40.167 --> 00:04:42.667
-Gross. Bizarre.

00:04:42.667 --> 00:04:44.801
Did you guys see this? Today, Elon Musk called off

00:04:44.801 --> 00:04:47.067
the launch of his Starship rocket

00:04:47.067 --> 00:04:49.067
due to a pressure issue.

00:04:49.067 --> 00:04:51.467
Yep. Elon tried to make the SpaceX team feel better.

00:04:51.467 --> 00:04:52.901
He was like, "Don't worry, guys.

00:04:52.901 --> 00:04:55.033
This rocket is still not as dangerous as driving a Tesla."

00:04:55.033 --> 00:04:56.868
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.868 --> 00:04:58.467
Well, a lot of people are talking about this.

00:04:58.467 --> 00:05:00.701
Netflix is apologizing after last night's

00:05:00.701 --> 00:05:02.934
"Love is Blind" live reunion.

00:05:02.934 --> 00:05:05.868
It was delayed due to technical issues.

00:05:05.868 --> 00:05:07.868
Yep. Even though they couldn't see the reunion,

00:05:07.868 --> 00:05:09.400
"Love is Blind" fans still managed

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:11.000
to fall in love with it anyway.

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:12.300
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:13.434
[ Woman laughing loudly ] Well, get this.

00:05:13.434 --> 00:05:14.734
I saw that -- Thank you.

00:05:14.734 --> 00:05:16.868
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.868 --> 00:05:19.701
That was a real good long laugh over on this side.

00:05:19.701 --> 00:05:21.901
I appreciate that. Guys, get this.

00:05:21.901 --> 00:05:25.367
I saw that Tupperware has warned that they are facing bankruptcy.

00:05:25.367 --> 00:05:26.534
-Ooh. [ Audience groans ]

00:05:26.534 --> 00:05:27.734
It's really gotten sad over there.

00:05:27.734 --> 00:05:28.901
When asked for a comment,

00:05:28.901 --> 00:05:31.100
the C.E.O. of Tupperware just burped.

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:35.634
[ Laughter ]

00:05:35.634 --> 00:05:37.701
Apparently, someone borrowed all their inventory

00:05:37.701 --> 00:05:38.834
and never gave it back. That's right.

00:05:38.834 --> 00:05:40.601
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.601 --> 00:05:42.501
The company said that they were never the same after that

00:05:42.501 --> 00:05:44.334
one time they used it for marinara sauce.

00:05:44.334 --> 00:05:47.234
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.234 --> 00:05:49.467
Guys, I heard that thieves in Philadelphia stole

00:05:49.467 --> 00:05:54.767
2 million dimes worth $200,000 from a truck parked at a mall.

00:05:54.767 --> 00:05:56.067
[ Laughter ]

00:05:56.067 --> 00:05:58.534
The suspects are described as armed and jingly.

00:05:58.534 --> 00:06:01.501
[ Laughter ]

00:06:01.501 --> 00:06:02.968
Oh, man, this is going viral.

00:06:02.968 --> 00:06:05.501
A man in North Carolina was relaxing on his patio

00:06:05.501 --> 00:06:08.200
when he had a surprise visitor. Take a look at this.

00:06:10.133 --> 00:06:12.334
[ Laughter, audience "Oohs" ]

00:06:18.334 --> 00:06:19.367
[ Bear grumbles ]

00:06:19.367 --> 00:06:23.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:25.934 --> 00:06:27.334
That's what every kid feels like

00:06:27.334 --> 00:06:29.267
when they run into their teacher at a supermarket.

00:06:29.267 --> 00:06:31.701
[ Laughter ]

00:06:31.701 --> 00:06:33.701
I'm not sure that clutching a throw pillow

00:06:33.701 --> 00:06:37.200
is how you protect yourself against a bear.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:39.033
Call me old fashioned, but I miss the good old days

00:06:39.033 --> 00:06:41.267
when bears used to do cocaine and rip your head off.

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:44.734
[ Laughter ]

00:06:44.734 --> 00:06:47.200
Finally, you guys, spring is here.

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:49.133
Okay? Are you feeling this? The weather...

00:06:49.133 --> 00:06:52.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:55.667
The weather is warming up. The flowers are in full bloom,

00:06:55.667 --> 00:06:57.467
which inspired me to write a song

00:06:57.467 --> 00:06:59.701
with one of our good friends, Andy Samberg.

00:06:59.701 --> 00:07:01.334
Here, take a look.

00:07:01.334 --> 00:07:03.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

